<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#villa-estate">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Villa (estate)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as villae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A villa, in the Carolingian context, was a great landed estate belonging to the church, the crown or the aristocracy. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> describe these villae as the primary units of agricultural production and local governance. Royal estates were regulated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitulary">capitulary</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitulare-de-villis">De Villis</a>, which set out how they were to be managed.</p></div>
